 "poem": "O'er the new moon's golden rim,\nAnd far up aloft above,\nThe stars from silver shimmerings creep,\nLike the dreams of a dreamer's fever.\nMiles and miles, like silver,\nThey trace their way across\nThe violet sky of the morning.\nOn the southern horizon they\nHang a curtain of silver.\nSome are in charge; some follow\nAs air fans on snow-white furze. etc.\nAs the young sun flies upward higher",
